WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.357
Hi, this is Tanmay Kulkarni,
in for Humanitarians AI.

00:00:03.735 --> 00:00:07.360
An essay I read this week says that
in 1983, technology "was not yet

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.064
a serious competitor" to any of
Howard Gardner's intelligences.

00:00:11.104 --> 00:00:13.820
So I went and read what Gardner
wrote later. He did ask.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.428
And he answered, one
intelligence at a time.

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:19.349
Think of his theory as a
house with eight rooms.

00:00:19.389 --> 00:00:23.775
Words, logic, space, music, the body,
nature, other people, and yourself.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:28.366
In October 2024, he and two colleagues
took machines through that house.

00:00:28.406 --> 00:00:32.518
A light only comes on where they say
a machine does what the room is for.

00:00:32.558 --> 00:00:34.041
Words and logic go first.

00:00:34.268 --> 00:00:37.729
Language models, they write, "clearly
exhibit the signs" of both. Two lights.

00:00:37.769 --> 00:00:39.478
Space: on, and that one surprised me,

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:42.293
because chess and Go are
filed there, not under logic.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:44.904
Music: on, even new pieces
in distinctive styles.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.915
The body, the room I'd
have bet stayed dark:

00:00:46.955 --> 00:00:49.147
programs that "adroitly" handle objects.

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:51.011
On. And nature: on. That's six.

00:00:52.025 --> 00:00:53.625
Two rooms are left, the personal ones,

00:00:53.645 --> 00:00:56.387
and here the paper says "one
should be more cautious."

00:00:56.427 --> 00:00:58.805
Other people, it leaves
ajar: it lists diplomacy,

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.813
salesmanship, therapeutic interactions.

00:01:00.853 --> 00:01:02.532
And knowing yourself stays dark.

00:01:02.572 --> 00:01:04.285
Using that word for a
program at all, they write,

00:01:04.305 --> 00:01:08.344
"can be seen as a 'category error.'" So
it isn't dark because a machine failed.

00:01:08.384 --> 00:01:11.993
It's dark because, on their reading,
the question doesn't apply.

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:15.673
So: six lights on, one door ajar,
one room dark on purpose.

00:01:15.988 --> 00:01:17.474
And that essay's sentence?

00:01:17.514 --> 00:01:19.540
The same paper's history of the field puts

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.134
programs doing logic
and math back in 1956,

00:01:22.602 --> 00:01:24.382
before the house was even built.

00:01:24.422 --> 00:01:27.252
So one of those lights may
have been on all along.

00:01:27.292 --> 00:01:28.792
The full video opens every door,

00:01:28.812 --> 00:01:32.979
and asks what it would take to switch
on room seven. It's linked right below.

00:01:33.019 --> 00:01:35.884
Tanmay Kulkarni, in for Humanitarians AI.
